==English==

===Etymology===
{{term|mop}} + {{term|up}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|phrasal verb|head=to [[mop]] up}}

# To [[clean up]] with a mop; especially to clean up a [[spill]] or [[mess]].
#: ''Please '''mop up''' the spilled milk.''
# {{idiomatic}} To fix [[problems]]; to [[correct]] or [[repair]].
#: ''After they argued, it fell to me to talk to her and try to '''mop up'''.''
